# Railway uploads the whole repository and then builds from the Root Directory.
# The scheduler in worker/ has ZERO dependencies and does not import a line of
# the Next.js app, yet the app's package-lock.json was travelling with it — and
# the dependency scanner reads that lockfile, so an advisory in a package the
# worker never loads was blocking the worker's deploy.
#
# Excluding everything but worker/ keeps the upload to a few kilobytes and gives
# the scanner only what the service actually runs.
#
# This file affects the Railway upload only. It has no effect on Vercel, which
# deploys the app from git.

